      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 2010 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "Sewing needles, albeit a rare case of penetrating cardiac injury, are potentially life-threatening. We report a case of a self-inflicted remnant intracardiac sewing needle which is diagnosed with nonspecific chest pain and successfully extracted 23 months after its insertion."
